CORE
main.c
--no-standard-checks
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^\[main.assertion.1\] .* shadow memory resolved: SUCCESS$
^\[main.assertion.2\] .* set: SUCCESS$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
Symbolic execution runs threads one after another, each starting with a copy
of its spawning thread's registry of shadow memory: an object that a thread
executed later allocates and publishes had no shadow memory for the earlier
one. The registrations of all threads and paths (of this and the previous
run of symbolic execution) are considered.
